   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region. Several stereocentres and the acyl chain length are inferred rather than read directly, as noted below.\n\n**Sequence, N-terminus to C-terminus:**\n1. Ac-Arg, with the guanidine drawn as NC(N)=N.\n2. A homocysteine-type residue (CH\u2013CH2CH2\u2013S) whose sulfur forms a thioether to the \u03b1-methylcysteine below.\n3. Asn.\n4. Thr.\n5. 7-Methyl-Trp.\n6. Lys, with its side-chain amine acylated by the linker described below.\n7. \u03b1-Methyl-Cys, quaternary and drawn with a hashed methyl. The ring runs from the homocysteine \u03b1-carbon through Asn, Thr, Trp and Lys to this residue and closes through the thioether.\n8. Tyr whose phenol oxygen carries a 2-aminoethyl group (OCH2CH2NH2).\n9. 2-Naphthylalanine.\n10. 4-Aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid, which is achiral.\n11. Glu, with a free side-chain acid.\n12. Asn.\n13. 3-Pyridylalanine.\n14. N-Methylglycinamide, N(C)CC(N)=O, as the C-terminal cap.\n\n**Lys side chain:** the amine carries two repeats of C(=O)CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013NH, which is the AEEA linker. These are followed by a \u03b3-Glu whose \u03b1-amine is acylated by a straight-chain fatty acid.\n\n**Uncertain points:**\n- **Stereochemistry:** I assigned L-configuration to every residue. I checked this against the drawn wedges for the Nal, Tyr and \u03b1-methyl-Cys centres. For the other residues I assumed L-configuration.\n- **Acyl chain length:** I estimated the fatty-acid length from pixel spacing and chose lauroyl (C12). The true chain could be a carbon or two shorter.\n\nSMILES: CC(=O)N[C@@H](CCCNC(N)=N)C(=O)N[C@H]1CCSC[C@@](C)(C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(OCCN)cc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc3ccccc3c2)C(=O)NC2(CCOCC2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2cccnc2)C(=O)N(C)CC(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](CCCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@H](NC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCC)C(=O)O)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc2c[nH]c3c(C)cccc23)NC(=O)[C@H]([C@@H](C)O)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(N)=O)NC1=O"
